# Fan out cheap candidates, then merge the shortlist into ONE flat context for a big model to pick.
# This is the thesis in miniature: a small model explores breadth; a big model judges — once.
#
# Run with two models (gen-runs passes them through as a pool):
#   ./gen-runs.sh range 7-7 model "small=<1B.gguf> big=<8B.gguf>" subdir ./runs/pick/
# (or a single model — :use falls through to it and the same flow still works).

:open examples/kv-bench-seed.chat.md

:use small
:fa 6 'Implement the change described above as one concrete Rust function. Just the function.'

# The six fan replies are the six most-recent leaves; reference them by relative position
# (-1 = last). In the GUI you'd instead click their highlighted ids, e.g. :mergectx a9j,3df,...
:use big
:mergectx -1,-2,-3,-4,-5,-6 'Pick the single strongest implementation. Name its id, then say why it wins.'

:export md
